# RFC#45 chunk 7 — per-image overhead correction for `PatchesData::is_cost_effective`

Commit:           HEAD (to be set on landing)
Host:             $(hostname)
Reference path:   ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--patches-chunk7-overhead
Codec-corpus:     ~/work/codec-corpus/gb82-sc + CID22-512/validation
Encoder mode:     Experimental (EncoderMode::Experimental)
Build:            cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder --example patches_gate_experimental_ab

## Background

W9-4 (chunk 6, commit 088719c5) relaxed the chunk-5 safety multiplier from
2.0x → 1.5x and admitted 4 of 6 previously-rejected high-d screenshot cells
on the experimental gate. Two residuals remained:
  - windows95.png @ d=4.0  (savings_est / total_overhead < 1.5x)
  - windows.png   @ d=4.0  (savings_est / total_overhead < 1.5x)

Per the W9-4 agent's note: "ref_overhead too large for any margin in
[1.0, 1.5] without breaking the 14 already-admitted cells. Queued for
chunk 7 (per-image overhead correction)." This commit ships chunk 7.

## Change

Pre-chunk-7 estimate of total overhead:

    total_overhead = ref_overhead       // trial-encoded reference frame
                   + dict_overhead_est  // analytical: 5 * ref_positions
                                        //           + 5 * positions

Chunk 7 swaps the analytical estimate for a real trial-encode of
`encode_patches_section`:

    total_overhead = ref_overhead       // trial-encoded reference frame
                   + dict_overhead      // trial-encoded dictionary section

The dictionary section is ANS-coded (8 contexts) with delta-encoded
per-occurrence positions, so the actual per-record byte count is much
smaller than the 5-byte analytical guess on screenshots with many similar
patches packed into a small reference frame. The analytical estimate was
overshooting `total_overhead` by 2-4x on those cells, inflating the
denominator of `savings_est / total_overhead` and forcing the chunk-6 1.5x
gate shut.

Chunk 7 also bundles the chunk-6 1.5x safety-margin relaxation (originally
authored as commit 088719c5 but never landed on main@origin). The two
changes ship together because chunk 7's per-image correction only matters
in conjunction with the relaxed margin.

## Bytes delta (negative = patches save bytes; 0 = gate rejected)

Compared to chunk-5 baseline
(benchmarks/patches_gate_experimental_ab_chunk5_2026-05-17.tsv):

Screenshot      d=0.5         d=1.0         d=2.0         d=4.0
windows95        same          same         -28768  NEW   -20961  NEW (RESIDUAL CLOSED)
terminal         same          same          same          same
codec_wiki       same          same          same         -10349  NEW
imac_g3          same          same          same        -157874  NEW
windows          same          same        -129035  NEW   -78806  NEW (RESIDUAL CLOSED)

Total newly-admitted savings: 425,793 B across 6 cells.
Both W9-4 residuals (windows95 d=4.0, windows d=4.0) are now admitted.

## 14 already-admitted cells (chunk 5)

All 14 stay admitted with byte-identical delta_B vs chunk-5 baseline.
(Note: the cells admitted by chunk 5 were a subset of the 6 newly-admitted
cells' siblings — chunk 5 admitted at lower d for the same images.)

## Photos (5 images x 4 distances = 20 cells)

delta_B = 0 on every photo cell. Detector returns None upstream for photo
content, gate not invoked.

